WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:34.806
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:35.076 --> 00:37.871
Did you find out who the person helping us is?

3
00:39.456 --> 00:40.457
What does he want in return?

4
00:44.461 --> 00:47.255
He can do that? And why does he want Chiara in return?

5
00:48.339 --> 00:49.215
What he wants

6
00:49.299 --> 00:52.427
is to overthrow the President of the Philippines.

7
00:54.846 --> 00:57.891
I just thought it would be better if I took the initiative

8
00:57.974 --> 01:00.769
and found out who this agency's enemies are.

9
01:03.480 --> 01:04.647
Tell me right away.

10
01:04.731 --> 01:06.483
Because I want to know what you're doing.

11
01:10.028 --> 01:11.821
He's not just some ordinary guy, sweetheart.

12
01:11.905 --> 01:14.532
Almost like the way Donatello and I used to move.

13
01:14.616 --> 01:17.077
I'm worried there might be another threat coming.

14
01:17.160 --> 01:18.828
Sweetheart. La Morte Bianca is gone.

15
01:18.912 --> 01:20.163
So just relax, okay?

16
01:20.246 --> 01:21.873
Nothing will get in our way anymore.

17
01:29.214 --> 01:31.716
He's not just planning to take down the Moravianos,

18
01:31.800 --> 01:35.970
he's slowly building Sinigang Cartel 2.0.

19
01:36.054 --> 01:39.808
So it's not just the senator we're watching.

20
01:39.891 --> 01:43.853
We're also watching a new syndicate being born.

21
01:45.688 --> 01:48.024
I thought you'd forgotten about me.

22
01:49.275 --> 01:50.944
You really know how to drop a punchline.

23
01:51.444 --> 01:53.780
I think you're spending too much time with that senator.

24
01:54.364 --> 01:55.740
So why did you call?

25
01:58.618 --> 02:00.078
And I hope you'll be honest this time.

26
02:05.792 --> 02:07.585
Will my family be left alone?

27
02:09.087 --> 02:11.798
Did you know more people get into accidents

28
02:12.298 --> 02:14.175
than get killed by syndicates?

29
02:14.759 --> 02:16.594
Norberto, don't give me that crap.

30
02:23.476 --> 02:25.728
Of all people, you should know

31
02:25.812 --> 02:28.648
that once you've stepped into a syndicate,

32
02:28.731 --> 02:32.861
you always have to watch your back.

33
02:44.455 --> 02:45.582
That's not true.

34
02:46.082 --> 02:46.958
Look at me.

35
02:47.041 --> 02:49.168
I got out of that messed-up life.

36
02:49.252 --> 02:52.505
Is that what you tell yourself every day?

37
02:57.010 --> 02:59.554
You did escape your messed-up life back then.

38
03:00.263 --> 03:03.558
But you know, it will catch up with you.

39
03:04.058 --> 03:05.685
So look at me.

40
03:07.312 --> 03:09.856
I chose to stay in the service.

41
03:09.939 --> 03:11.941
I chose to fight.

42
03:15.528 --> 03:18.323
I can't run from the wrongs I've done in my life.

43
03:18.406 --> 03:20.241
So here I am,

44
03:21.242 --> 03:25.580
facing my own ghosts from the past.

45
03:26.497 --> 03:27.665
Mario.

46
03:28.374 --> 03:31.669
No matter what happened between us,

47
03:33.212 --> 03:35.798
I still consider you a friend.

48
03:38.259 --> 03:41.846
Not just as a friend, but as a father.

49
03:43.598 --> 03:46.726
As soon as I get any information

50
03:47.227 --> 03:52.273
that says there's a threat or danger to Mikoy and Chiara's lives,

51
03:54.692 --> 03:57.278
you'll be the very first to know.

52
03:57.862 --> 03:59.364
Thank you, my friend.

53
03:59.447 --> 04:00.531
I look forward to it.

54
04:13.253 --> 04:14.254
Rahmboy!

55
04:16.297 --> 04:18.716
-Brothers. -Whoa!

56
04:18.800 --> 04:20.260
You're getting good at chopping!

57
04:20.343 --> 04:22.637
The axe doesn't even get stuck in the wood anymore.

58
04:23.554 --> 04:25.390
Mario taught me, Mikoy.

59
04:26.891 --> 04:29.227
He said you can't just keep chopping away.

60
04:29.310 --> 04:31.896
You've got to position yourself right and know where to put your force.

61
04:32.480 --> 04:35.441
And there's also a timing to splitting the wood.

62
04:35.525 --> 04:37.694
It's like dancing, right, guys?

63
04:37.777 --> 04:41.155
-You need the right rhythm. -What a punchline.

64
04:41.239 --> 04:43.241
You know, it's kind of like life.

65
04:43.324 --> 04:44.784
Right? Sometimes,

66
04:44.867 --> 04:47.495
life is just life.

67
04:47.996 --> 04:48.871
-That was lame! -That was lame!

68
04:49.831 --> 04:50.665
-Come on. -What was that?

69
04:50.748 --> 04:52.959
That made no sense. I thought it was going somewhere.

70
04:57.171 --> 04:58.756
Hey, wait. Why'd you stop?

71
05:00.174 --> 05:03.219
No, bro. I was just happy for you guys.

72
05:03.720 --> 05:06.848
You guys just seem so happy, like you don't have a care in the world.

73
05:08.850 --> 05:10.435
No, that's just how we are.

74
05:10.518 --> 05:12.186
-Yes. -That's how we were raised.

75
05:12.270 --> 05:14.022
Not just by our parents,

76
05:14.105 --> 05:16.858
but by our neighbors, our friends,

77
05:16.941 --> 05:18.151
even the people we know.

78
05:18.943 --> 05:21.821
And it's not that hard to be happy even in the middle of problems.

79
05:21.904 --> 05:25.658
As long as I don't have toxic people around me.

80
05:25.742 --> 05:27.243
That's the best part.

81
05:27.327 --> 05:28.328
You guys are so fun.

82
05:29.162 --> 05:30.997
I hope I get to experience that too.

83
05:33.333 --> 05:35.084
He's getting all emotional!

84
05:35.168 --> 05:36.085
So sentimental!

85
05:37.378 --> 05:38.755
What, are you gonna open up now?

86
05:38.838 --> 05:40.590
What, are we having an open forum now?

87
05:40.673 --> 05:41.674
-Yes. -Go ahead.

88
05:41.758 --> 05:44.552
-It's just us anyway. We're all guys here. -Exactly.

89
05:47.638 --> 05:49.724
No, I just miss my mom.

90
05:57.398 --> 05:59.358
Where is your mother, Rahmboy?

91
06:01.736 --> 06:03.529
She's an OFW, in Hong Kong.

92
06:04.572 --> 06:05.740
Hong Kong, huh?

93
06:05.823 --> 06:07.575
Chiara and I just got back from there.

94
06:07.658 --> 06:09.827
We might've even seen your mother there.

95
06:10.828 --> 06:12.080
That was five years ago, bro.

96
06:13.289 --> 06:15.166
-Is that so? -Oh, five years ago.

97
06:16.167 --> 06:17.085
So where is she now?

98
06:21.631 --> 06:22.465
My mom.

99
06:24.133 --> 06:27.136
Hello, Mom. We miss you!

100
06:27.720 --> 06:28.971
Mom, I'm a size 10!

101
06:30.556 --> 06:33.768
-Ma, I'm a size 7! -What size 7?

102
06:33.851 --> 06:35.770
You guys, seriously. Here, take this.

103
06:35.853 --> 06:39.023
These guys might ask her to send them money next.

104
06:39.107 --> 06:40.108
Thank you, bro.

105
06:40.191 --> 06:41.609
Ma, sorry it's so noisy.

106
06:41.692 --> 06:44.654
I'm fine. I'm with them.

107
06:47.657 --> 06:49.575
-Oh, no! -Why?

108
06:49.659 --> 06:52.912
My fiancée left her water bottle behind again.

109
06:52.995 --> 06:54.413
I need to deliver it to her.

110
06:55.331 --> 06:57.166
-What, is there no water there? -Exactly.

111
06:57.250 --> 06:58.501
You guys don't get it.

112
06:58.584 --> 07:02.130
Her water bottle has lemon, chia seeds, psyllium husk,

113
07:02.213 --> 07:05.675
collagen, electrolytes, ginkgo biloba, and Shirota strain.

114
07:05.758 --> 07:07.552
If she doesn't drink that,

115
07:07.635 --> 07:09.595
I'm sure we're all screwed again.

116
07:09.679 --> 07:10.763
-We're screwed? -We're screwed?

117
07:10.847 --> 07:12.265
Of course, you're coming down with me!

118
07:12.348 --> 07:15.935
Where's her water bottle with all that stuff you mentioned?

119
07:16.018 --> 07:17.019
There it is.

120
07:17.103 --> 07:17.979
Let's find it.

121
07:18.062 --> 07:19.188
Let's go!

122
07:19.272 --> 07:20.857
Goodness!

123
07:22.275 --> 07:26.988
Agent Alex, I'm so excited to see Chiara wearing her wedding gown.

124
07:27.071 --> 07:30.199
So this is what it feels like when someone in the family is getting married.

125
07:30.283 --> 07:31.993
You know, Agent,

126
07:32.076 --> 07:34.245
I feel like I'm the one getting married.

127
07:34.328 --> 07:35.788
Is that normal?

128
07:35.872 --> 07:37.373
Of course, Miss Tess.

129
07:37.457 --> 07:39.459
You've grown attached to Chiara too.

130
07:39.542 --> 07:40.918
And you've come to think of her as your daughter too.

131
07:41.002 --> 07:41.752
Exactly.

132
07:41.836 --> 07:43.838
So in a sense, it's like your daughter who's getting married too.

133
07:44.422 --> 07:45.339
Exactly.

134
07:46.966 --> 07:47.967
Mom!

135
07:49.385 --> 07:50.887
Mikoy, what are you doing here?

136
07:50.970 --> 07:54.056
-Are you the one fitting the gown? -No, Mom.

137
07:54.140 --> 07:55.975
Chiara texted me.

138
07:56.058 --> 07:57.810
She left her water bottle behind.

139
07:57.894 --> 07:59.103
You know how it is.

140
07:59.729 --> 08:01.397
That bottle is basically her emotional support bottle.

141
08:01.481 --> 08:05.276
She might transform if she doesn't get to do her little water regimen, right?

142
08:05.359 --> 08:06.652
Oh, right.

143
08:08.738 --> 08:09.947
Miss Tess, Chiara's calling you.

144
08:10.031 --> 08:12.617
My other daughter is calling me. I'll leave you two for now.

145
08:21.209 --> 08:22.043
Hey.

146
08:23.920 --> 08:24.962
Thanks, okay?

147
08:26.464 --> 08:27.757
For what now?

148
08:27.840 --> 08:30.218
Lately, you keep thanking me.

149
08:32.136 --> 08:33.054
For everything.

150
08:34.138 --> 08:35.097
For being here.

151
08:35.598 --> 08:37.266
For things like this.

152
08:38.809 --> 08:40.603
Because Chiara doesn't always have to hear

153
08:40.686 --> 08:43.147
my opinion, right?

154
08:43.689 --> 08:47.068
It's important that she can talk to people outside our relationship.

155
08:47.151 --> 08:48.778
People who aren't my relatives.

156
08:49.278 --> 08:51.739
Like you. Right?

157
08:53.199 --> 08:55.743
So she can let out all the stress she's dealing with in life.

158
08:56.619 --> 08:57.703
Even if it's about me.

159
08:59.539 --> 09:00.581
You know?

160
09:01.082 --> 09:03.251
In short, so she's free to bash you.

161
09:04.919 --> 09:06.337
Pretty much.

162
09:07.171 --> 09:08.839
But I'm not perfect, you know?

163
09:08.923 --> 09:11.842
Of course I'm in love with Chiara, but I'm not perfect.

164
09:12.885 --> 09:15.471
Of course, there are things I might do that she won't like.

165
09:16.722 --> 09:19.600
I don't want her to keep all of that to herself.

166
09:22.019 --> 09:23.854
You two really are perfect for each other.

167
09:30.653 --> 09:31.779
Thank you, Alex.

168
09:36.450 --> 09:39.078
Guys, Chiara's ready!

169
09:39.161 --> 09:41.205
Mikoy, why are you still here?

170
09:41.289 --> 09:44.208
You can't see Chiara wearing her wedding gown.

171
09:44.292 --> 09:45.126
It's bad luck.

172
09:45.209 --> 09:48.254
Your mom's right. Come on, Mikoy, go for now.

173
09:48.337 --> 09:50.172
-Okay, just give this to Chiara. -Sure.

174
09:50.756 --> 09:51.924
Go on.

175
09:52.008 --> 09:55.344
-Leonela, come on. Come with me. -Go ahead, Miss Tess.

176
10:44.727 --> 10:46.520
Oh, no, Mikoy! You're not allowed to look!

177
10:46.604 --> 10:47.438
It's bad luck!

178
10:53.152 --> 10:55.655
Did I come to the right building?

179
10:57.073 --> 10:59.241
The place is right, and so is the schedule.

180
11:00.117 --> 11:02.328
But why does something feel wrong?

181
11:02.411 --> 11:04.914
Did I miss an announcement?

182
11:06.540 --> 11:07.375
You got that right.

183
11:08.209 --> 11:09.794
You missed the announcement that there's no meeting today.

184
11:11.754 --> 11:12.797
I knew it.

185
11:12.880 --> 11:14.965
So you knew there was no meeting?

186
11:16.258 --> 11:19.428
I knew it. I'm the newest one to get kicked out of the group chat,

187
11:19.512 --> 11:22.556
then they made a new group chat and didn't invite me.

188
11:23.140 --> 11:24.892
It's so annoying. It pisses me off.

189
11:27.812 --> 11:28.854
I've got your back.

190
11:29.814 --> 11:32.191
I'll get updates from your classmates,

191
11:32.274 --> 11:35.152
then I'll DM you if there are any special announcements like this.

192
11:35.653 --> 11:37.113
And you know what?

193
11:37.196 --> 11:39.990
Sometimes it's better to have fewer group chats.

194
11:40.074 --> 11:42.159
Because think about it, all you'll see

195
11:42.743 --> 11:45.955
is nonstop noise, gossip, and spam messages anyway.

196
11:46.038 --> 11:46.872
It's better this way.

197
11:47.373 --> 11:50.042
Thank you, Laurence, for offering to help, but you know,

198
11:50.126 --> 11:51.210
I can handle this.

199
11:53.087 --> 11:54.880
I know who's behind all this.

200
11:54.964 --> 11:56.507
It's that girl.

201
11:57.842 --> 12:00.136
Why should I adjust when I'm the one being bullied?

202
12:00.219 --> 12:02.304
And why should I be scared?

203
12:02.388 --> 12:04.223
Just because I got kicked out of the group chat?

204
12:08.727 --> 12:10.062
Luisa Mae.

205
12:12.440 --> 12:14.442
-So, did it arrive? -It did.

206
12:31.667 --> 12:34.628
Oh, sweetheart, you look absolutely beautiful!

207
12:34.712 --> 12:36.881
Your wedding gown looks perfect on you.

208
12:44.346 --> 12:47.433
One step closer to becoming Mrs. Pinagpala.

209
12:49.768 --> 12:52.813
And one step closer to the life you've always dreamed of.

210
12:52.897 --> 12:54.565
A life that used to be just a dream.

211
12:54.648 --> 12:56.400
You prayed for it, and look at you now.

212
12:56.484 --> 12:58.903
There you are, already wearing your wedding gown.

213
13:01.489 --> 13:04.408
It's just sad that you're not here, Ma, Pa.

214
13:05.034 --> 13:07.953
I know this was a dream for you too, but…

215
13:08.454 --> 13:10.831
it's okay even if you're not here.

216
13:10.915 --> 13:13.709
I can still feel how much you love me.

217
13:15.002 --> 13:18.255
Darling, I still need to make some adjustments to your wedding gown.

218
13:18.839 --> 13:22.092
I'm not satisfied yet, and I'm still not happy with it.

219
13:22.176 --> 13:24.720
Oh, sweetheart, your seamstress seems like a perfectionist.

220
13:24.803 --> 13:26.305
That's a good thing because if it were me,

221
13:26.388 --> 13:28.724
I'd want every adjustment to be perfect too.

222
13:28.807 --> 13:31.727
So have her fix it until your wedding gown is perfect, okay?

223
13:31.810 --> 13:34.104
Yes, your mama is right, sweetheart.

224
13:41.904 --> 13:43.614
-I love you, sweetheart! -I love you, sweetheart!

225
13:44.823 --> 13:45.783
I'll give this to Mommy Tess.

226
13:45.866 --> 13:47.284
‎And a little bit longer.

227
13:47.368 --> 13:49.495
Chiara, Chiara, come here for a moment.

228
13:49.578 --> 13:52.331
It looks like someone wants to have a few things changed,

229
13:52.414 --> 13:55.334
some things added or altered. Alex has a few suggestions.

230
13:55.417 --> 13:57.795
It's up to you if you want to, but I was thinking it might look better if…

231
14:07.638 --> 14:10.432
Where's Viktor? He has a delivery from the senator.

232
14:13.394 --> 14:14.270
Huh?!

233
14:14.770 --> 14:17.147
Are you looking for Sir Viktor?

234
14:17.231 --> 14:20.568
Why are you shouting? I'm right in front of you.

235
14:22.403 --> 14:24.864
When I was taking a shower earlier,

236
14:24.947 --> 14:28.409
I think water got into my ear.

237
14:28.492 --> 14:32.788
So I'm not sure if I'm speaking too softly

238
14:32.872 --> 14:34.790
or too loudly.

239
14:34.874 --> 14:37.960
Are you looking for Sir Viktor?

240
14:38.043 --> 14:39.003
Yes.

241
14:39.670 --> 14:41.171
Sir Viktor!

242
14:46.844 --> 14:47.845
What is it?

243
14:48.762 --> 14:50.806
Here it is, right?

244
14:50.890 --> 14:52.391
We're almost there.

245
14:52.474 --> 14:54.768
We'll officially be in-laws soon.

246
14:55.436 --> 14:58.647
After everything we've been through,

247
14:58.731 --> 15:02.109
our families really are getting a happy ending.

248
15:02.860 --> 15:03.903
Thank you, in-law.

249
15:03.986 --> 15:06.447
For being there for Chiara,

250
15:07.156 --> 15:09.742
while we're here, and I'm here,

251
15:10.367 --> 15:12.786
paying for the sins of a married couple.

252
15:14.163 --> 15:16.540
Thank you for taking care of her,

253
15:16.624 --> 15:17.917
for listening to her.

254
15:19.001 --> 15:22.254
For being there when it should've been me, because I'm her mother.

255
15:22.338 --> 15:24.590
Oh, in-law.

256
15:24.673 --> 15:26.926
Chiara is like a daughter to me now.

257
15:27.468 --> 15:29.553
You know, she's not hard to love.

258
15:30.304 --> 15:32.640
She's not hard to take care of either.

259
15:32.723 --> 15:36.435
Didn't I tell you? We'll make it to our happy ending.

260
15:36.518 --> 15:37.937
And besides, hello?

261
15:38.020 --> 15:40.606
Don't worry, I am so sure

262
15:40.689 --> 15:43.400
you'll see each other and be together again.

263
15:44.068 --> 15:45.778
Our families are getting a happy ending,

264
15:45.861 --> 15:50.115
and you're going to have a happy ending where you're crying and feeling sad?

265
15:58.082 --> 15:59.333
Hey, Luisa Mae.

266
15:59.416 --> 16:02.127
Enough with pretending to be the sweet girl, nice girl,

267
16:02.211 --> 16:04.171
and good girl.

268
16:10.511 --> 16:13.305
And you actually brought a sidekick.

269
16:18.644 --> 16:19.728
Seriously?

270
16:20.270 --> 16:21.605
Don't you have any originality?

271
16:28.278 --> 16:31.699
So you might as well know your place.

272
16:31.782 --> 16:33.367
I'll know my place, all right.

273
16:36.245 --> 16:39.123
And, you know, I'm protecting myself too,

274
16:39.206 --> 16:41.709
and that's called self-defense.

275
16:41.792 --> 16:44.753
And what you did by kicking me out of the group chat,

276
16:44.837 --> 16:46.338
that's bullying.

277
16:46.880 --> 16:50.718
And I won't let you just do whatever you want to me,

278
16:50.801 --> 16:52.302
especially when it's wrong.

279
16:52.386 --> 16:53.637
So, can you?

280
16:54.221 --> 16:55.055
Enough.

281
17:01.061 --> 17:04.523
Well, you don't get to tell me when to stop

282
17:04.606 --> 17:07.943
because I'm just getting started, Sofie.

283
17:13.365 --> 17:15.075
Because starting today,

284
17:15.826 --> 17:20.539
you, Sofia Anikka Ruiz,

285
17:20.622 --> 17:24.001
are considered a persona non grata.

286
17:24.585 --> 17:26.879
What the hell is a persona non grata?

287
17:26.962 --> 17:31.383
Are you the city or something and you have executive power?

288
17:31.467 --> 17:33.177
Wow, that's a lot!

289
17:40.184 --> 17:43.854
If you don't like the term "persona non grata",

290
17:44.354 --> 17:46.356
fine, let's make it simple.

291
17:55.824 --> 17:59.828
You know, you really have no originality.

292
18:00.329 --> 18:01.830
That's from F4.

293
18:06.335 --> 18:08.629
You know what? That's enough.

294
18:14.760 --> 18:19.139
You know, that's the price you pay for messing with the queen bee.

295
18:19.973 --> 18:21.475
And you know what? You're right.

296
18:57.052 --> 18:58.720
Okay, what's the plan?

297
18:58.804 --> 19:00.681
Why do we have to be in formation?

298
19:01.640 --> 19:04.685
-Nothing. Discreet matters. -Okay.

299
19:05.185 --> 19:07.437
Discreet? Why does it have to be discreet?

300
19:09.523 --> 19:12.276
Because we're planning your stag party, bro.

301
19:12.359 --> 19:13.527
Right?

302
19:13.610 --> 19:15.112
Wait, are you guys serious?

303
19:16.029 --> 19:17.281
No, I don't want that.

304
19:18.198 --> 19:19.116
Why?

305
19:22.619 --> 19:23.579
Wait, wait.

306
19:23.662 --> 19:25.080
Then why is he still here?

307
19:25.164 --> 19:26.290
-Exactly. -This is a surprise.

308
19:26.373 --> 19:28.542
-This is a surprise. You're not invited. -Go inside, go inside.

309
19:28.625 --> 19:30.460
Bro, wait. Go inside. We'll call you later. Just wait.

310
19:31.753 --> 19:33.964
Okay, here. Here's our plan.

311
19:34.047 --> 19:37.092
Just keep in mind our budget, 1,500 only, so we can have more.

312
19:37.176 --> 19:38.010
Yes.

313
19:38.093 --> 19:40.053
-Is that possible? -That's enough money.

314
19:41.013 --> 19:42.681
Don't cry, my love.

315
19:45.142 --> 19:47.352
Everything will be all right.

316
19:48.645 --> 19:50.856
We'll get out of here eventually.

317
19:54.026 --> 19:55.360
I know.

318
19:56.862 --> 19:58.780
I just can't accept that as her mother,

319
19:59.781 --> 20:01.825
I'm not by my daughter's side

320
20:01.909 --> 20:04.203
for the most important event of her life.

321
20:04.286 --> 20:07.122
We won't even be able to attend her wedding.

322
20:17.382 --> 20:20.761
But we have to be happy for her.

323
20:23.347 --> 20:27.434
So that she won't be sad either.

324
20:28.936 --> 20:30.062
I know that.

325
20:30.562 --> 20:32.314
There's nothing we can do

326
20:33.607 --> 20:35.734
but be happy for her.

327
20:47.329 --> 20:50.374
You need to come with us, Viktor Valtrovi.

328
20:52.376 --> 20:54.211
-Take him. -What? Why?

329
20:54.294 --> 20:55.462
-What's going on? -Where are you taking him?

330
20:55.545 --> 20:57.673
-Where are you taking my husband? -Where are you taking me?

331
20:57.756 --> 21:00.175
Hey, wait! Explain yourselves.

332
21:00.259 --> 21:01.218
Come with us.

333
21:01.843 --> 21:03.220
Where are you taking him?

334
21:05.138 --> 21:06.640
What, aren't you going to answer?

335
21:06.723 --> 21:09.059
-Where are you taking my husband? -Hey! What's going on?

336
21:09.142 --> 21:10.227
-Don't worry. -What is it this time?

337
21:10.310 --> 21:13.730
-Viktor! Where are you taking my husband? -Where are you taking Sir Viktor?

338
21:13.814 --> 21:15.565
-Hang on! -Viktor!

339
21:15.649 --> 21:17.567
Don't worry, ma'am. I'll take care of Sir Viktor.

340
21:17.651 --> 21:18.610
Sir Viktor!

341
21:18.694 --> 21:19.861
-Viktor! -Hey!

342
21:22.114 --> 21:23.991
Wait!

343
21:25.158 --> 21:26.535
I'm Sir Viktor's plus-one.

344
21:27.119 --> 21:28.996
We're like B1 and B2!

345
21:29.079 --> 21:30.622
We're always together.

346
21:30.706 --> 21:33.542
Wherever he is, I'm there!

347
21:33.625 --> 21:34.835
Remember that!

348
21:34.918 --> 21:36.461
Suit yourself!

349
21:36.545 --> 21:40.632
Then you two can suffer together with no relief in sight. Get in!

350
21:40.716 --> 21:42.384
-Okay, okay. Easy. -Go!

351
21:42.467 --> 21:43.552
Come on.

352
21:47.806 --> 21:50.267
So there we go. We're all set, okay?

353
21:52.352 --> 21:53.979
Thank you!

354
21:54.479 --> 21:57.441
So, Chiara, are you okay with the changes we added?

355
21:57.524 --> 22:00.277
Of course. Actually, I'm so thankful to you.

356
22:00.360 --> 22:03.238
My fairy maid of honor.

357
22:03.322 --> 22:05.824
Because I've really been nervous about my wedding,

358
22:05.907 --> 22:07.659
but because all of you are here for me,

359
22:07.743 --> 22:08.827
I'm excited now.

360
22:09.786 --> 22:12.956
I'm sure you'll be the most beautiful woman on that day.

361
22:14.624 --> 22:17.419
Leonela, come on. Come with us.

362
22:17.502 --> 22:19.046
Oh, no. You guys go ahead. Go ahead.

363
22:19.129 --> 22:20.380
I still have somewhere to go.

364
22:20.464 --> 22:22.090
I have something to take care of with the catering.

365
22:22.174 --> 22:23.633
Thank you so much.

366
22:23.717 --> 22:25.469
-Thank you, thank you, everyone. -Thank you. We'll go ahead.

367
22:26.553 --> 22:27.721
Take care.

368
22:30.724 --> 22:31.767
You're here?

369
22:33.643 --> 22:34.978
Do you need me to pick you up?

370
22:38.315 --> 22:41.193
How about this? Let's not see each other yet, okay?

371
23:02.422 --> 23:04.049
Hey, Carlota.

372
23:04.674 --> 23:06.343
What are you doing here?

373
23:07.344 --> 23:08.970
Waiting for you.

374
23:09.054 --> 23:10.680
Didn't I tell you to meet me here?

375
23:10.764 --> 23:12.182
So we could go in together.

376
23:12.265 --> 23:14.559
Okay, sure. Shall we?

377
23:15.143 --> 23:15.936
Shall we?

378
23:21.858 --> 23:23.527
GLOBAL AGENCY FOR GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS

379
24:07.070 --> 24:09.156
Did you know it's been a while since I last had a foot spa?

380
24:11.908 --> 24:14.035
But believe me, this call is an urgent matter.

381
24:14.119 --> 24:17.873
I have an update about that video and that mysterious vigilante.

382
24:20.333 --> 24:22.794
-Mario, Captain is looking for you. -Why? Did something happen?

383
24:22.878 --> 24:24.796
It's about the Manananggal?

384
24:24.880 --> 24:26.756
I'll just change my clothes.

385
24:26.840 --> 24:29.593
-And I'll follow you to barangay hall. -All right.

386
24:30.385 --> 24:33.013
-About that again. -And why the rush?

387
24:43.148 --> 24:44.733
Who were you talking to earlier?

388
24:44.816 --> 24:46.318
What are you hiding, Sianong?

389
24:46.401 --> 24:49.738
Why do I only see your red flags now?

390
24:53.909 --> 24:54.743
Mom?

391
24:58.205 --> 25:00.081
Mama Yaya?
